WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.161
I kept buying courses. One looked
useful and was on sale, so I bought it.

2
00:00:04.812 --> 00:00:06.815
Then another. And another.

3
00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:08.870
I watched a few lessons,

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.680
but I kept buying more courses
than I had time to watch.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.106
Now those courses were
sitting in my account, unused.

6
00:00:15.146 --> 00:00:16.680
Had I wasted that money?

7
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.582
The information was still useful.

8
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:19.813
I needed a way to use it.

9
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.837
Here's a three-step method I call CAP:

10
00:00:22.877 --> 00:00:25.792
Capture, Arrange, Put to work.

11
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.295
Step one: Capture. Get the captions:

12
00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:31.220
the words spoken in the lessons.

13
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.470
You need a computer, internet
access and a few browser skills.

14
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:36.988
I will show you the steps.

15
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.090
Open Developer Tools in your
browser and choose Network.

16
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.000
With recording on,
reload the Udemy lesson,

17
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.980
turn on captions and play the video.

18
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.792
then save the recording
in a file called HAR.

19
00:00:49.832 --> 00:00:52.740
This manual method still
takes playback time.

20
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.113
Ask AI to pull out the
captions in the file.

21
00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:56.860
Keep the lesson names and times.

22
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.290
Step two: Arrange. Sort the text
by course, topic and lesson.

23
00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.700
Make a simple index showing what each
lesson covers and where to find it.

24
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.460
Now you have a course
library you can use again.

25
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:16.966
Step three: Put it to work. Choose the
useful parts and tell AI what you need.

26
00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.460
Ask it to explain a topic, give you
an exercise, or help with a project.

27
00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.060
You can also make your
own notes and checklists.

28
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.985
Say I want to make a mobile app.

29
00:01:26.025 --> 00:01:29.540
I can give AI the course
text and describe my idea.

30
00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.524
Then ask it to help me plan the
app and show which lessons it used,

31
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.222
so I can check the answer.

32
00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:38.970
The Udemy Caption Kit
is seventeen dollars.

33
00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:42.066
You get the full CAP steps,
prompts to copy and paste,

34
00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.045
and files to organise your lessons.

35
00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:47.710
Choose Get the Caption Kit below.

36
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:52.845
For Hotmart, Domestika or another course
website, join the free waiting list.

37
00:01:52.885 --> 00:01:56.950
Ask for a guide, a tool to
help collect captions, or both.

38
00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.495
Your requests help me
choose what to build.

39
00:01:59.535 --> 00:02:01.421
I will let you know if
it becomes available.
